"""
port_probe.py  -  Isaac Sim 6, run from Window > Script Editor.

The jointed borescope (PhysX articulation) driven by YOUR kinematic model (spatial_borescope_model.py),
placed IN THE ENGINE at the inspection port, with the calibrated tip camera + LED.
Same probe as model_driven_probe.py: the model's frame (origin at the port, +Y into the engine, +Z up)
is simply put on the port. Open the engine first (engine_textured.usd), then run this.

    world --fixed--> PortBase --2-axis PIVOT at the port (probe tilt)--> Pivot --prismatic (PUSH, lambda)-->
    Carriage --revolute (ROLL about the probe axis)--> Tube_00
    Tube_00 ... Tube_N   capsule links, 2 revolute joints (X, Z) per junction with a bending spring (passive cable)
    Neck_00 ... Neck_11  capsule links, 2 revolute joints (X, Z) per junction with position drives (the bending neck)
    Head                 rigid camera head (20 mm) + tip camera

The cable is pushed through the port: the part behind the port slides in, it is not teleported.
Every physics step the model gives the targets: push (lambda), axial rotation, and the neck joint angles that put
each neck link along the model's neck arc. PhysX moves the joints; the script reads where the neck end and the
camera really are and compares them with the model (printed at the end).

Gravity: GRAVITY = False (pure kinematics test). True = the tube sags with the bench-calibrated stiffness.
"""

